#entry("agent-A:WP-14", "interface", status: "final")[*Place search: find a building, floor or room by name (for B's search box and C's CityStage focus).* Contract in `@ibasho/core`: `PlaceHit { kind: 'building' | 'storey' | 'room'; id; name; aliases: string[]; buildingId; buildingName; storeyId?; city (pack id, e.g. 'city-hyderabad'); tile?: [tx, ty]; centre: [x, y] (place frame mm, the pack frame for the samples); bbox: { minX, minY, maxX, maxY } mm; heightRange?: { lo, hi } mm (building height range, or storey floor to top); source: 'osm' | 'document' | 'merged'; contextIds? (OSM ids a document replaces: hide them when focusing); score 0 to 100; matched: string[] (names that matched, for highlighting) }` and `PlaceSearchOptions { limit? (10), kinds?, city?, buildingId?, minScore? (30) }`.
Implementation in `@ibasho/plan` (pure, offline, fast enough per keystroke): `const index = buildPlaceIndex({ cities: [{ city: 'city-hyderabad', tiles }], buildings: [{ doc, city: 'city-hyderabad', contextIds: HERO_CONTEXT_IDS.gb1 }] })` then `searchPlaces(index, query, opts?) => PlaceHit[]` (ranked: exact, prefix, token and fuzzy (edit distance 1 or 2); case and diacritic insensitive; every query word must match). Tiles come from `loadCityTiles()` of `@ibasho/pack-city-hyderabad/engine` and `@ibasho/pack-city-london/engine`; documents from `@ibasho/fixtures/buildings/<id>.building.json` (or the store). Names indexed: OSM `name`, `alt_name`, `short_name`, `official_name`, `name:en`, `old_name`, `loc_name`, `addr:*` (now kept in the tiles as `ContextBuilding.aliases` and `.addr`), curated campus names (`CURATED_ALIASES`: Vindhya Bhavan, Himalaya, Nilgiri, KCIS for Kohli Research Block, OBH, NBH, Bakul, Parijaat, AIMSCS, ...), storey names plus "floor N", "level N", "LN", "Nth floor", ordinals, "basement" or "cellar", and room names plus their function (e.g. "A3 lab"). Examples that work (tests): "Vindhya", "vindya", "VINDH", "KCIS", "Himalaya", "Vindhya floor 2" (storey Second floor), "A3 lab" (rooms), "vindhya cellar". Also exported: `normaliseName`, `editDistance`, `CURATED_ALIASES`.]

#entry("builder:WP-07 (agent C)", "interface", status: "final")[*`<CityStage>` for the studio (agent B mounts it).* `import { CityStage, type CityStageProps, type CityStageHandle } from '@ibasho/scene'`; it fills a sized parent. All props optional; with none it shows the Vindhya stand in on the stand in IIIT campus, 21 March 10:30. Source of truth: `packages/scene/src/city/CityStage.tsx` and `src/city/types.ts`.
- Data: `place?: { lat, lon, tzHours?, name? }`; `tiles?: CityTile[]`; `roads?`; `hero?: BuildingDoc | null`; `compiled?: CompiledBuilding | null` (hero drawn from `meshes`, lens ids exact); `site?: SiteResult | null` (radiation and facade sun hours per surface id); `daylight?: DaylightGrid[] | null`; `lanterns?: LanternDatum[]`; `stamp?: ResultStamp | null`. Rule: `undefined` = labelled scene estimate (Preview), `null` = not computed yet (nothing painted).
- View: `level?` / `onLevelChange?` (`city | site | building | floor | room`), `storeyId?`, `roomId?`, `onSelect?(CityTarget)`; `lens?` / `onLensChange?` (`none | shadows | sun-hours | radiation | daylight | lanterns`); `time?: { date: 'YYYY-MM-DD', minutes }` / `onTimeChange?`; `azimuthDeg?` / `onAzimuthChange?`. Each is controlled when given.
- Moments: `sweep?: { dates, key }` + `onSweepEnd?` (1); `penumbra?` (default true) and `heightOverrides?: Record<contextId, mm>` closes a band (2); radiation wick (3, automatic); daylight drawer at Floor level (4); `phototropic?: { t, canopyTiltDeg?, finDepthM?, steps? }` (6); `style: 'yoru'` or lens `lanterns` (8).
- Find (owner request): `focus?: { kind: 'building' | 'storey' | 'room', buildingId, storeyId?, roomId?, bboxMm?: { minX, minY, maxX, maxY } } | null` with `onFocusChange?`, and `ref.current.flyTo(focus | null)`. Eases the camera (cut under reduced motion), outlines in ink by day or lights by night, dims the rest, and for a storey or room lifts the floors above away (cutaway). A hero id maps to Building, Floor or Room; a context id frames that neighbour; any other id uses `bboxMm` (map a `PlaceHit` bbox here); unknown with no bbox does nothing. Choosing a ladder level clears the focus. `resolveFocus()` is exported for the search UI.
- Shell: `style?: 'washi' | 'yoru' | 'svg'`, `reducedMotion?`, `tierCap?` (default 2), `llmGenerating?`, `controls?` (default true: ladder, lens chips, time strip, legend; set false and drive by props), `legend?`, `legendFor()` for an external legend, `stats?`.
- Requests to WP-00 (core): add `DaylightGrid` (per storey sDA and ASE point grid) and `LanternDatum` to `core/v3`; confirm the `BuildingDoc.rotationMdeg` convention used here: plan +y points to that bearing clockwise from true north. Agent A: `packs/city-hyderabad` tiles drop straight into `tiles`.]
