#entry("agent-A:WP-13+WP-17", "interface", status: "final")[*Design before you build (SPEC 27), platform part.* All additive.
- *London plots on demand:* `@ibasho/pack-city-london/engine` exports `cityLondonKingsCross`, `loadKingsCrossTiles(read?)`, `KINGS_CROSS_TILE_FILES` and `CITY_AREAS` (`city-london` default, `city-london-kings-cross` on demand; 611 buildings, 184 with tagged levels or heights, 694 trees, about 52 KB). Place `pl_kings_cross` ("King's Cross, London", `onDemand: true`, `codePackIds: ['codes-uk']`, no buildings yet: place designed buildings there; its own frame from 51.5352 N, 0.1250 W).
- *Codes by plot location:* `codePacksFor` gives `codes-uk` for UK places and `codes-in` for India when a place lists none. New buildings in England get `UK.PARTL.ENERGY` (design EUI against the Part L 2021 notional, ratio band), `UK.PARTL.FABRIC` (unknown until constructions are set), `UK.FHS.2025` (fails with gas heating; else ratio against the Future Homes notional with a heat pump), `UK.PARTO.GLAZING` (dwellings, simplified method, high risk in central London) and in Greater London `LONDON.PLAN.SI2` (35% on-site saving for major developments) and `LONDON.PLAN.BE-LEAN`. Baseline row `Part L 2021`. Existing UK homes (permit before 2022-06-15) keep `UK.EPC.ESTIMATE` only. Indian plots unchanged. `EnergyParams.heatPumpScop` (heat pump for heating and hot water) is new.
- *Typed targets with gaps (AC-PD3):* core `Goal` gains `{ kind: 'net-zero-ready'; basis: 'uk-nzcbs' | 'fhs-2025' | 'london-plan' | 'in-nzeb' }` and `{ kind: 'lowest-opex' }`; `GoalGap { presetId?, goal, status: 'met' | 'not-met' | 'unknown', value?, target?, unit?, ruleIds?, reason, sources, grade }`; `GOAL_PRESETS` (ids `net-zero-ready-uk`, `fhs-2025`, `part-l`, `london-plan`, `ecsbc-super`, `leed-gold`, `lowest-opex`, each with sources and regions). Pass `JobInputs.goals`; the codes stage returns `CodesOut.gaps` (schema updated). `lowest-opex` needs the optimiser: call `goalGaps(goals, { codes, ratings, baselines, energy, optimise })` from `@ibasho/preview` after the optimise stage. LEED levels stay `unknown` (only the energy credit is estimated); ECSBC tiers read the EPI ratio (Compliant 1, Plus 0.85, Super 0.7, estimates).
- *Placement (AC-PD2):* `placementChange(prev, next)` gives `none`, `move`, `rotate` or `design`; `stagesForPlacementChange(kind)` the stages to rerun. A move reuses the compiled geometry (only placement and hash change, no recompile), so the geometry stage is instant and the sun onward reruns with the new context; pass the previous outputs as `JobInputs.previous`.]

